SUMMARY:Mountains-to-Sea Trail Highway 25 toward Bent Creek
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Mountains-to-Sea Trail Hiking Club 2.0\nThis is a fa
 irly easy hike\, and we go at a high average to low advanced speed\, which
  is roughly about 3.0 to 3.2 mph. There are no super long hills. It's pret
 ty undulating all the way.\n\nWell behaved dogs on leashes are welcome to 
 attend.\n\nWhen you arrive\, park at the gravel lot across from the trail 
 head. You'll see some people gathering by their cars. I've recently correc
 ted the PIN setting on the map\, so it should be correct. Here are some di
 rections to use too: When going south on Hendersonville Road\, go past Car
 olina Day School and turn right at the Blue Ridge Parkway exit. When you g
 et to the parkway turn RIGHT. You will see parking on the left and right s
 ide of the road. Park there.\n\nMountains-to-Sea-Trail hikes are designed 
 for fitness and community among people who are already reasonably fit. It'
 s not an endurance hike by any means\, but it is designed so we can get ou
 r hearts beating a bit while still being able to have a conversation and m
 eet new people.\nWhen you arrive\, we'll circle up and introduce ourselves
  briefly.\n\nWe leave the parking spot at 9:10. If someone needs a nature 
 break\, we wait fo you\, but it's not a hike where we stop and take photos
  or frequent breaks. We basically keep hiking until the 1/2 way mark\, the
 n turn around after a short (approximately 5 minute) break. Then we keep t
 hat same pace on the way back. If we get on a trail right at 9:10\, we are
  normally finished around 10:50.\n\nThese are out and back hikes\, meaning
  that we hike in and turn around half way to return back.
